## Two Types of Tasks: Instant vs Timed

This is a fundamental addition to Showd. Tasks now have an optional duration. This creates two distinct flows through the app:

### Instant Tasks (no duration set)
Examples: Take medication, drink water, check email, take vitamins.
These are quick actions — either you did it or you didn't. The flow is unchanged from the current app:
```
Reminder fires → Done / Snooze / Struggling
```

### Timed Tasks (duration set)
Examples: Exercise for 30 min, study for 1 hour, meditate for 15 min, deep work for 2 hours.
These take time to complete. Tapping "Done" immediately would be a lie — you haven't done it yet. The flow is:
```
Reminder fires → Start / Snooze / Struggling
  ↓ Start tapped
Focus Timer counting down (can pause, can tap Done early, can Struggle)
  ↓ Timer hits 0:00
Post-Timer Reminder (full-screen) → Done / Extend (with limits) / Struggling
  ↓ If extended
Timer restarts with extension time
  ↓ All extensions used + timer hits 0:00
Post-Timer Reminder → Done / Struggling only (no more extensions)
```

**The duration is optional per task.** During task creation, the user can set a duration or leave it blank. If no duration is set, the task behaves exactly as it does today.

