## Edge Cases & Error Handling

**Network offline:**
- Task creation works offline (Supabase has offline support via local cache / optimistic updates). Syncs when back online.
- Reminders ALWAYS fire — they're local notifications, no network needed.
- Done/Snooze/Struggling responses queued locally, synced when online.
- Focus timer runs entirely locally — no network dependency.

**App killed / force stopped:**
- Android: Foreground service + boot receiver reschedules notifications.
- iOS: Notifications survive app kill. Reconcile on reopen.
- **NEW — Active timer killed:** If the app is killed mid-timer, the persistent notification remains (Android). When user reopens app, check for task_events with status 'in_progress'. If found, calculate elapsed time and resume the timer from where it left off.

**User changes timezone:**
- Detect on app open, recalculate all notification schedules.
- Update user's timezone in Supabase.

**User uninstalls and reinstalls:**
- Supabase Auth session can be recovered with phone number re-verification.
- All data in Supabase — fully recoverable.
- Re-register all local notifications on first open.
- Active timers from previous install are gone — mark any orphaned in_progress events as missed via the scheduled Edge Function.

**Multiple reminders at same time:**
- Queue and show sequentially with "1 of 2 reminders" indicator.

**Witness sends nudge (future feature):**
- Plan the data model now (nudges table is ready).
- Witness web page could have "Send a message" button.
- Nudge appears on reminder screen.

**Two users witness each other:**
- Fully supported. Separate witness_connections each direction.

**User changes witness:**
- Old witness_connection marked 'removed' → "ended" SMS → new invite flow.

**Task with past time:**
- Daily task at 8 AM created at 3 PM → first reminder tomorrow 8 AM.
- "Once" task with past date → show error, don't allow.

**NEW — Timed task edge cases:**
- User starts timer then phone dies → on recharge + app open, check in_progress events, offer to resume or mark as missed.
- User has two timed tasks at the same time → first one's reminder fires, Start it, second one queues. When first completes, second's reminder fires.
- User sets 5-min duration on a task → short timer, only 2 extensions available (+5m, +10m max).

